# Third-party material in Spoolworks

`LICENSE` grants MIT terms over the **original** work in this repository. Several files are not
original and are not ours to license. This file itemises them.

**This is a good-faith inventory, not legal advice.** The unresolved item below is a real obstacle
to redistribution and should be settled before any public release.

---

## 1. DnG-Crafts/K2-RFID — UNRESOLVED

<https://github.com/DnG-Crafts/K2-RFID>

Spoolworks began as the macOS port in that project (contributed back as its PR #51). **Upstream
publishes no LICENSE file**, so its material carries default copyright — all rights reserved — and
no grant to redistribute.

Verbatim upstream files still in this tree:

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `reference/arduino-aes/AES.cpp`, `AES.h` | ESP32 firmware AES, used by `Tools/aes-reference-check.sh` to generate golden test vectors |
| `reference/colors.db` | The Windows app's colour database (see §2 for its own contents) |
| `reference/app-icon.ico` | The Windows app's icon, currently a placeholder |

The Swift source is a **reverse-engineered reimplementation**, not a copy. `SPEC/` and the doc
comments cite upstream file and line numbers as an evidence trail for how the tag format was
established; those are references to upstream, not reproductions of it.

**To resolve:** ask DnG-Crafts to declare a licence. Failing that, the three files above have to be
removed — which costs the golden-vector check, the colour-table regeneration and the icon — or
replaced with independently obtained equivalents.

## 2. meodai/color-names

<https://github.com/meodai/color-names> — MIT licensed.

The colour-name dataset inside `reference/colors.db`, and therefore the derived
`Sources/SpoolworksCore/Resources/colors.bin` (31,861 named colours). MIT permits redistribution
with attribution; this notice is that attribution. Note that the *packaging* of the dataset into
`colors.db` is upstream's work and falls under §1.

## 3. Creality

Material databases and printer files, produced by Creality and neither ours nor upstream's to
license:

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `Sources/SpoolworksCore/Resources/{k1,k2,hi}.json` | Bundled material catalogues, shipped in the app |
| `reference/seeds/{k1,k2,hi}.json` | Their provenance copies |
| `reference/printer-dumps/*.json` | Files pulled off a K2 Plus, including the `material_box_info.json` used as a test fixture |

These are factual data about Creality hardware, read from devices the user owns. That is a weaker
basis for a copyright claim than creative work, but it is not nothing, and it is not covered by
this repository's MIT grant.

## 4. Design

The Modernist design system and the `Spoolworks` screen designs came from a Claude Design handoff
bundle commissioned by the repository owner. The handoff files themselves are not in this
repository; only the SwiftUI implementation is, and that implementation is original work under
`LICENSE`.

